          "Here are some questions to help you tell the difference, honestly and before God (Ps 139:23-24). <strong>What do I want?</strong> If I want to win, humiliate, or prove I am better, that is likely pride. If I want truth, safety, fairness or a healthier relationship, that is likely self-respect or a boundary.",
          "<strong>How am I speaking?</strong> Pride tends to be contemptuous, sarcastic or loud; it attacks the person. Self-respect tends to be calm, clear and specific; it addresses the behaviour. <strong>Can I admit my part?</strong> Pride struggles to say “I was wrong too.” Self-respect can own its part without collapsing. <strong>Would I accept this from them?</strong> If I would want the same freedom to say no, to be heard, or to set a limit, then I am asking for something fair, not special.",
